| Item | Why it may change |
| --- | --- |
| `status` (`StatusResponse`, `StatusItem`, `Health`) | No consumer has used it |
| `PartialSuccess`, `FailedOp`, `CompletedOp`, `SkippedOp` | Widened with the op index per [Spec 07](07-wisp-and-monokl-envelope.md) §4; still no consumer |
| `AlreadyDone`, `already_done()` (Node `alreadyDone`) | The check half of the idempotency design; no caller yet |
| `Sensitive<T>` | A redaction wrapper no renderer takes yet |
| `telemetry::NoopProvider` | A placeholder for an observability seam |
| `Dag::ready_by_edge` and edge kinds | New in 0.7; the argument order has changed once already |
| The `schemars` feature | JSON Schemas for MCP `outputSchema`; no consumer yet |
| `michi-pipeline`: `ExecutionError` variants, `StepObserver`, `DurableObserver`, `ExecOptions` defaults | Nothing runs pipelines yet |
| `michi-pipeline` `serde` shape of `RunRecord` | Callers persist it, so any change is called out in the changeset and old records are reported, never misread |
| `RecoveryHint.params` as a list of pairs | A representation choice that may become typed (`structured_content` became `Option<JsonObject>`) |

// michi_core::audience
#[non_exhaustive]
pub enum Audience { Assistant, User } // serde: "assistant" / "user"

// michi_core::telemetry
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default)]
pub struct NoopProvider;
impl NoopProvider {
    pub fn span(&self, name: &str);             // no-op
    pub fn count(&self, name: &str, value: u64); // no-op
}
```

The structs above are `#[non_exhaustive]` from 0.4.0: build them with their constructors, then read or assign their public fields as before (`PartialSuccess` is read through its getters). Struct literals and exhaustive destructuring work only inside michi-core, so adding a field later is not a breaking change. `Value`, `KvValue`, `AlreadyDone`, `RetryConfigError` and the other enums marked `#[non_exhaustive]` above need a `_` arm in a `match` outside michi-core.

/// Repeatable response sections.
pub mod section;
/// Health and status response rendering.
pub mod status;
/// No-op telemetry provider.
pub mod telemetry;
/// TOON list rendering, the token-optimized list format.
pub mod toon;
/// UTF-8 char-boundary-safe truncation within one string.
mod.rs

